@startuml ABU-SSO Use Case Diagram
title ABU-SSO — Central Identity Provider and Campus Services
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam actorStyle awesome
actor Student
actor Staff
actor Admin
actor "Campus OIDC Client" as Client
rectangle "Central ABU-SSO Identity Provider" {
  usecase "Authenticate with matric/staff number" as UCLogin
  usecase "Maintain / revoke central IdP session" as UCSession
  usecase "View own profile" as UCProfile
  usecase "View digital ID card" as UCID
  usecase "Manage campus wallet" as UCWallet
  usecase "View own Login & Security Activity" as UCActivity
  usecase "Read own security notifications" as UCNotify
  usecase "Administer users and clients" as UCAdmin
  usecase "Inspect system-wide authentication audit" as UCAudit
  usecase "Register and validate OIDC client callbacks" as UCRegistry
}
rectangle "Six Independent Campus Applications" {
  usecase "Start OIDC Authorization Code Flow" as UCOIDC
  usecase "Create service-local session" as UCLocal
  usecase "Revalidate central session" as UCRevalidate
  usecase "Access protected campus service" as UCProtected
}
Student --> UCLogin
Student --> UCSession
Student --> UCProfile
Student --> UCID
Student --> UCWallet
Student --> UCActivity
Student --> UCNotify
Staff --> UCLogin
Staff --> UCSession
Staff --> UCProfile
Staff --> UCID
Staff --> UCWallet
Staff --> UCActivity
Staff --> UCNotify
Admin --> UCAdmin
Admin --> UCAudit
Admin --> UCRegistry
Client --> UCOIDC
Client --> UCLocal
Client --> UCRevalidate
Client --> UCProtected
UCOIDC .> UCSession : checks central session
UCLocal .> UCOIDC : after successful authorization
UCProtected .> UCRevalidate : requires current authorization
note right of UCActivity
  Users can view only their own
  login, service-access and
  security-notification records.
  Notifications retain read/unread state.
end note
note right of UCAudit
  Administrators have system-wide
  authentication audit visibility.
end note
note bottom of UCProtected
  Campus Wi-Fi is represented as a browser-based
  OIDC portal. RADIUS / 802.1X network enforcement
  is outside this prototype's scope.
end note
@enduml
